## ACTIVE TASK

- D5 — Auth Entry Flow: Google + Login + Magic Link + Safe Redirects — VERIFY &
  SHIP, on branch `d5-auth-entry-flow`, created from `origin/main` at
  `68282dc4d0205964403bfe87b704690990c3797a`. `origin/main` had not advanced at
  verification time, so that commit is also the branch merge-base.
- Auth errors now have one closed application vocabulary, in the new pure module
  `frontend-next/src/lib/auth/errori-auth.ts`: eleven codes, one Italian message
  each, plus `classificaErroreAuth` for Supabase failures and
  `classificaErroreProvider` for an OAuth return. No provider or Supabase text
  reaches the user any more. `auth-service.ts` returns a code instead of
  `error.message`, and the previous "not configured" string that named the two
  environment variables and their file is gone.
- `/auth/callback` stays server-side and keeps `exchangeCodeForSession`, the
  server-resolved public origin and the relative-redirect guard. Its five
  returns are unchanged in shape; what travels in the redirect is now only
  `?errore=<codice>`. The technical detail goes to `console.error`
  `[auth/callback]` on the server and is never serialized into the URL.
- The flow remembers where it started. `/accedi` and `/registrati` declare their
  own `superficie`, it travels in the validated `redirectTo` query and the
  callback returns to `PERCORSO_SUPERFICIE_AUTH[superficie]`, so a Google error
  begun on `/registrati` no longer lands on `/accedi`.
- There is one destination contract, not a second one: `PARAMETRO_NEXT`, always
  relative and always validated by the existing `percorsoRelativoSicuro`, with
  `/home` as fallback. Absolute, protocol-relative and malformed values are
  dropped. Password login, magic link and the OAuth round trip share it, and
  `/vendite` now asks to come back to itself through it. No cookie, no
  `localStorage`, no trust in an absolute URL from the browser.
- `/accedi` distinguishes which operation is running (`"password" |
  "magic-link" | null`) instead of one shared boolean, and the Google button
  owns its own start state. Each gesture has its own error slot and clears only
  its own; an error still named in the URL is discarded on the next attempt, so
  it cannot reappear later. No operation can start twice, and a failure releases
  the control for an immediate retry. Google reads `Continua con Google` on
  `/accedi` and `Registrati con Google` on `/registrati`.
- An authenticated visitor still sees no active form and is not redirected
  automatically; the proposed destination is the requested `next` and logout
  stays available.
- Every private gate that stops a visitor now also says where to bring them
  back. `/vendite` already did; VERIFY added the same shape to `/account`,
  `/cantina`, `/completa-profilo` and `/vendi`, each with its own written
  destination and never one deduced from incoming data. `/checkout/[id]` was
  deliberately left as it was: its destination is dynamic and reconstructing it
  from the route id could send the visitor to the wrong listing. `/home` was
  left alone because its `next` would be the fallback itself.
- The audit of the BUILD diff found no concrete defect in the error, redirect,
  coordination, AgeGate or Facebook confirmations, so nothing was corrected
  under that heading; the entry-point gap above is the only functional change
  VERIFY added.
- Twenty-two files changed inside `frontend-next/`: nineteen modified plus three
  new (`src/lib/auth/errori-auth.ts` and the two test files
  `src/lib/auth/errori-auth.test.ts` and `src/lib/auth/flusso-ingresso.test.ts`).
  Outside `frontend-next/` the change set is `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and
  `CHANGES.log`.
- Full validation, all executed: the targeted `bun test src/lib/auth/` produced
  **93 pass / 0 fail / 479 expect() calls across 4 files**; the full
  `frontend-next` suite produced **989 pass / 0 fail / 18,379 expect() calls
  across 59 files**; `bun run lint` reported zero errors and 13 pre-existing
  unrelated warnings; `bun run typecheck` and `bun run build` were clean;
  `git diff --check` was clean. `/accedi`, `/registrati`, `/account`,
  `/cantina`, `/completa-profilo` and `/vendi` still prerender static;
  `/auth/callback` and `/vendite` stay dynamic.
- CI `MIN_TESTS` was raised from **929** to the measured **989**, in
  `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and in the contract assertion that mirrors it in
  `src/lib/beta/prelaunch-contract.test.ts`.
- The Supabase Redirect URLs allowlist was re-measured read-only before ship,
  with the non-mutating `GET /auth/v1/verify` probe on project
  `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej`: the plain callback, the callback with `?next=...` and
  the callback with `?superficie=...&next=...` were each echoed back verbatim
  with the query preserved, while an `evil.example.com` control fell back to the
  Site URL. The wildcard is in place and the query-carrying `redirectTo` is not
  silently rewritten.
- No migration, schema, RLS, grant or production write. No Supabase, Google
  Console, environment or provider change. Facebook stays absent, the D4
  AgeGate/DOB path is untouched, no legal consent is inferred from a Google
  click and the Google-plus-password model stays undecided.

